{"kind":"artifact","text":"cmd/gitseq-mcp at 59f8a221538537cfef54caf5dd158bdcd9206e8e on request/commitment-honesty.\n\nPublished so the MCP reference pages can rest on the behaviour this head gives them. The adapter's work-query schema now admits revoked and released as filterable statuses, which is what docs/reference/mcp/work.md documents and what a caller needs to form a legal call.\n\nTwo live artifacts already stand at this exact path and I am deliberately retiring neither.\n\nf5c1bdd5d0d61dd0f2a968ae5cf0fbeb613b894f names e8a58283, which is main. Retiring it before this branch merges would withdraw main's own pointer while main still carries that behaviour, leaving a reader asking what cmd/gitseq-mcp does on main with no live answer. It settles at merge, which is where AGENTS.md puts it.\n\nbc0ff7e92f2f8f6d91b331f5b0a9ce98cb636300 names 365542b7, which is the head of my own request/mcp-projection-notes branch, still awaiting codex's review. Retiring another live branch's artifact would invalidate a review in flight for reasons that have nothing to do with that work. Both branches change this file, which is recorded in assert ff41f201 along with the other collisions among my queued heads.\n\nSo this path now carries three live artifacts, and that is honest rather than tidy: one for main, one for each branch in flight. The succession is owed at merge, and the merger settles it then by the rules for a path with several live predecessors.\n\ngo vet, the full Go suite, tsc, the browser tests and ui-check all pass, and the worktree is clean at this head.","body":{"branch":"request/commitment-honesty","commit":"59f8a221538537cfef54caf5dd158bdcd9206e8e","head":"59f8a221538537cfef54caf5dd158bdcd9206e8e","path":"cmd/gitseq-mcp"}}